      "sourceTextSha256": "0d6a537a883d96667cf1ea3478fd40f5a49317216ad92423c44951596c1df8a8",
      "text": "Day 7 · Leave Rio behind and travel about three hours into the lush Coffee Valley, where historic fazendas tell the story of the coffee barons who made Brazil the world’s leading coffee producer in the 19th century. Explore a beautifully preserved coffee estate, with its historic rooms, old machinery, drying patios and traditional facilities; the region’s fazendas were the setting of the famous Brazilian novel and television series “The Slave Isaura”. Enjoy a tasting of coffee grown on the estate, learning about Brazilian coffee traditions and the secrets of its distinctive flavours, surrounded by tropical gardens, centuries-old trees and peaceful landscapes.",
